1
00:00:00,130 --> 00:00:03,290
Your pension owns things you would never buy.

2
00:00:03,290 --> 00:00:04,843
And nobody asked you.

3
00:00:04,843 --> 00:00:05,483
Not once.

4
00:00:05,483 --> 00:00:08,315
You were opted in. Including into this.

5
00:00:08,315 --> 00:00:11,765
Pension. Four-oh-one-k. Workplace plan.

6
00:00:11,765 --> 00:00:13,025
Same machine.

7
00:00:13,025 --> 00:00:14,915
When you joined, you chose a number.

8
00:00:14,915 --> 00:00:16,265
How much goes in.

9
00:00:16,265 --> 00:00:19,245
You almost certainly never chose where it goes.

10
00:00:19,245 --> 00:00:21,115
That is the default fund.

11
00:00:21,115 --> 00:00:22,955
Most people never move.

12
00:00:22,955 --> 00:00:25,725
So what is actually in it?

13
00:00:25,725 --> 00:00:29,105
An index. A basket of the largest listed companies.

14
00:00:29,105 --> 00:00:33,215
Bought automatically. By size. No judgement.

15
00:00:33,215 --> 00:00:36,345
Nobody screens it. That is the entire point of it.

16
00:00:36,345 --> 00:00:38,525
So look at what the basket holds.

17
00:00:38,525 --> 00:00:42,445
Banks and insurers. One of the biggest slices in it.

18
00:00:42,445 --> 00:00:46,715
Alcohol. Gambling. Tobacco. Weapons.

19
00:00:46,715 --> 00:00:49,455
Not by accident. By construction.

20
00:00:49,455 --> 00:00:51,545
And the banks are the sharp part.

21
00:00:51,545 --> 00:00:53,695
A bank's product is not a service.

22
00:00:53,695 --> 00:00:54,955
It is interest.

23
00:00:54,955 --> 00:00:57,245
Own the bank, own the income.

24
00:00:57,245 --> 00:01:00,815
That is not a technicality. That is the whole business.

25
00:01:00,815 --> 00:01:03,825
But here is the part almost nobody knows.

26
00:01:03,825 --> 00:01:06,985
Your fund is built to change as you age.

27
00:01:06,985 --> 00:01:10,865
They call it lifestyling. Or a glide path.

28
00:01:10,865 --> 00:01:12,625
It sounds like safety.

29
00:01:12,625 --> 00:01:14,755
The closer you get to retiring...

30
00:01:14,755 --> 00:01:16,965
...the more it sells shares...

31
00:01:16,965 --> 00:01:18,965
...and buys bonds.

32
00:01:18,965 --> 00:01:20,915
And a bond is a loan.

33
00:01:20,915 --> 00:01:24,025
You are lending money. At interest.

34
00:01:24,025 --> 00:01:27,435
The machine moves you deeper into it as you get older.

35
00:01:27,435 --> 00:01:32,725
Automatically. Quietly. As a feature you were never shown.

36
00:01:32,725 --> 00:01:35,785
So. Two minutes. Three steps.

37
00:01:35,785 --> 00:01:39,405
One. Log in. Find the name of your fund.

38
00:01:39,405 --> 00:01:45,195
If it says default, balanced, or a retirement year — that is the basket.

39
00:01:45,195 --> 00:01:48,625
Two. Search that fund's largest holdings.

40
00:01:48,625 --> 00:01:51,455
You will recognise the banks immediately.

41
00:01:51,455 --> 00:01:57,585
Three. Open the full fund list. Look for a sharia or Islamic option.

42
00:01:57,585 --> 00:02:01,575
Most workplace schemes have one now. Switching is usually free.

43
00:02:01,575 --> 00:02:06,015
Same contributions. Same employer match. Different basket.

44
00:02:06,015 --> 00:02:08,195
You were opted in by default.

45
00:02:08,195 --> 00:02:13,085
Default is still a choice. Somebody else just made it for you.

46
00:02:13,085 --> 00:02:15,440
Two minutes. Go and make it yourself.
